<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panduranga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Panduranga was the southernmost region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, around modern Phan Rang and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phan-thiet">Phan Thiết</a> in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. After the Vietnamese conquest of Vijaya in 1471 it became the last centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> kingship, surviving as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a> and later of the Nguyễn dynasty until its final annexation in 1832.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panduranga.jpg" alt="Panduranga" width="320" height="624" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Balkrishna Kulkarni. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syayambhuvithoba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
